==Battleground==
*1 [[Li'l Bun Bun]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Li'l Bun Bun]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Li'l Bun Bun]] spawns after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Li'l Bun Bun]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*5 [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Zir Zeal]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
If you have any Ubers that can deliver massive damage to the Bun Buns, like [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Windy]] or [[Strike Unit R.E.I. (Uber Rare Cat)|R.E.I.]], this level will be a piece of cake for you, as all enemies here spawn on a timer. Barring this, a highly levelled (30~45) [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] with [[Cat Combo|Strong Up]] combos and the support of [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]/[[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necrodancer Cat]] and proper protection from [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] and Dual Erasers is enough to nullify the danger of this stage. You can cheese this stage by stalling the Li'l Bun Buns with [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] and meatshields, before letting [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] slowly kill everything and advance on to the base.

You also can use [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]] with [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]. Along with a few meatshields, they will be very effective against the Li'l Bun Buns. Ideally, the Zombies will burrow past your units, but it is good to bring units to fight the Zombies in case they approach your base before the enemy base is destroyed.

